WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.268
Ukraine's counteroffensive

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:04.170
is into its second month

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.406
and progress has been slow.

00:00:07.107 --> 00:00:08.408
The challenges are vast.

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:09.876
Russia's war in Ukraine

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:10.744
is the world's

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:12.679
largest armed conflict

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:14.714
since World War Two.

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:16.549
This war is being fought on the ground

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:17.817
with traditional weaponry

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:19.619
like tanks and bullets.

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:21.855
But also in the skies

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:24.090
with newer technologies like drones.

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:27.560
A report in May found Ukraine was losing

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:30.964
more than 10,000 drones per month.

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:34.801
Well, my next guest says swarms of drones

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:37.370
are the future of war.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.672
Eric Schmidt ran Google for many years,

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:42.308
but more recently advised the Pentagon

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:43.843
as the chair of the Defense

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.311
Innovation Board.

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:46.079
He now chairs

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:48.415
the special Competitive Studies Project,

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.717
a think tank focused on technology

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:52.352
and national security.

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:52.952
I should note,

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:55.221
I am a senior advisor to Schmidt Futures,

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:57.057
his philanthropic initiative.

00:00:58.358 --> 00:01:00.260
Eric Schmidt pleasure to have you.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.628
Good to be back.

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:04.597
So you were recently in Ukraine

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:05.765
and a lot of

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:08.101
your concerns stemmed from that

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:10.036
Let's first

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:12.705
just get a sense of the lay of the land.

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:13.940
What to you,

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.608
what does the battlefield look like?

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:17.510
Who has the advantage?

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.778
The thing that's shocking

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.013
is how big this war

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:22.415
is, 2000 kilometers long.

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:24.250
And since 2014,

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:24.818
the Russian

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:26.519
side has dug themselves in

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:28.588
in this horrific way.

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:30.657
So if you were a Ukrainian soldier

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:31.291
with your commander

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:33.159
saying go across this

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:35.161
five kilometer disputed area,

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:37.931
you'd have to get through the tanks.

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:40.100
The mines, the machine

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.001
guns, their drones.

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:43.436
You get to the other side,

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:44.971
you do your killing.

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:46.239
And then the back

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:48.274
part of Russia kills you.

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:50.210
It's an insurmountable task.

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:52.112
I was stunned

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:52.712
to read

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:55.014
how many shells the Russians are using.

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:58.485
60,000 a day The world

00:01:58.485 --> 00:01:59.686
production in the West

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:01.788
can accommodate about 5000 a day.

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:02.789
I guess the Russians have been

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:04.824
building artillery for about 50 years.

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:06.593
And they have an infinite supply.

00:02:06.593 --> 00:02:08.561
60,000 a day now.

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:08.928
I mean,

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:09.395
my math

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:10.230
is that you're talking about

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:12.665
something like 20 million a year.

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:14.234
Is too easy today.

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:16.903
This is a World War One, artillery war.

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:19.272
With people dug in.

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:20.440
How incredible.

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:21.541
100 years later,

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:23.576
we haven't come up with another way.

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:24.811
If you're the Ukrainians

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:26.212
trying to break through,

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:28.081
you want to get to the Sea of Azov.

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:29.149
You have to break through this

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:29.849
initial line

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:31.718
blows up reserve, for example,

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:33.286
and then you have to make a corridor.

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:34.787
Well, as you go through your corridor,

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:36.022
they're bombing you as well.

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:38.057
And now the bombing is precision bombing.

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:38.324
Right,

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:40.560
because you can target more accurately.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.262
And the American doctrine

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:43.663
is that you would always do

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:45.865
such infantry moves with air power,

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:47.200
which the Ukrainians don't have.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.301
And the air power comes

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:49.702
in, cleans the path,

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:50.870
and then the American gets

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:52.872
gets the other side running back,

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:53.973
and then they start to win.

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.543
We, meaning the Ukrainians,

00:02:56.543 --> 00:02:57.076
the U.S.,

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:59.112
the West, need a solution

00:02:59.112 --> 00:03:00.880
to get them moving.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.782
So that gets us to drones.

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:04.317
They are already using

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:06.186
an extraordinary number of drones

00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:07.220
the Ukrainians.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.454
How many drones are they?

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:11.257
Are they using a week or a month?

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:12.926
They're on track to using a couple

00:03:12.926 --> 00:03:14.961
hundred thousand drones in a year.

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:16.229
Most drones

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:18.264
only survive one or two flights

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:20.700
before they fail or they're blocked.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:21.768
I was shocked

00:03:21.768 --> 00:03:22.702
at how good

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:23.203
the Russians

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:25.338
were at electronic warfare and jamming,

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:26.940
basically everything

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:28.474
you send into this battlefield,

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:30.410
which is quite narrow, by the way,

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:31.878
the rest of the country is fine.

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:34.681
I suspect on both sides they jam.

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:36.382
Everything is jam

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:38.418
but also communications is jammed.

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:40.053
So normal drones don't work.

00:03:40.053 --> 00:03:41.454
So the Ukrainians have

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:43.122
taken cheap Jones and added

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:45.091
additional antenna antennas.

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:46.626
One of things that I learned

00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:48.795
was something called a kamikaze drone,

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:50.863
which is a $400 Chinese drone

00:03:50.863 --> 00:03:52.465
that carries a small payload.

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:54.467
It moves so fast you can't shoot it down.

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.236
I had thought that

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:58.071
that was the innovation of the war.

00:03:58.071 --> 00:03:59.439
To generals yesterday

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:01.507
told me that I'm wrong

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:03.276
and that what they really need

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:04.844
are cruise missile drones,

00:04:04.844 --> 00:04:06.412
which can go really far

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:07.547
and carry with wings

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:09.148
and can carry more payloads.

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:09.882
I don't think

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:11.117
the Ukrainian drone strategy

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:12.585
is completely formed,

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:13.253
but they're building

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:15.722
a completely new theory of war

00:04:15.722 --> 00:04:16.789
and this is where

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:18.391
we get to the solution for you.

00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:19.993
The only way the Ukrainians

00:04:19.993 --> 00:04:20.627
can break through

00:04:20.627 --> 00:04:21.361
these lines

00:04:21.361 --> 00:04:23.830
is with massive numbers of drones,

00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:25.431
massive number of drones,

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:27.900
or massive number of human casualties

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.168
on both sides.

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:30.570
The beauty of the drone is

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:31.871
it can take out the other side's

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:32.672
military target

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:34.574
without collateral damage.

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:35.174
Right.

00:04:35.208 --> 00:04:37.143
We are very concerned about the

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:38.244
the propagation

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:40.079
of this war against other countries,

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:41.014
but I'm very concerned

00:04:41.014 --> 00:04:42.382
about its effect on civilians,

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:44.250
both the Russians and Ukrainians.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:45.285
The important thing about a drone

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:47.453
is it's a very, very targeted solution.

00:04:47.654 --> 00:04:49.088
It's very inexpensive.

00:04:50.056 --> 00:04:50.657
I think

00:04:50.657 --> 00:04:52.659
the goal that we should have for Ukraine

00:04:52.659 --> 00:04:54.460
is to establish the principle

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:56.696
that there will never be another land war

00:04:56.863 --> 00:04:59.098
where you can invade successfully,

00:04:59.599 --> 00:05:01.434
that we're respecting the land.

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:03.703
The sovereignty of the land is important.

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:05.605
If you're mad at them, that's fine.

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:06.339
You can negotiate,

00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:07.407
you can put pressure,

00:05:07.407 --> 00:05:09.142
but you can't send artillery

00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:10.677
and flattened cities,

00:05:10.677 --> 00:05:11.210
which is what

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:13.179
the Russians have been doing.

00:05:13.613 --> 00:05:14.914
How do you get

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:15.281
how do you

00:05:15.281 --> 00:05:16.783
how do you get to the solution of

00:05:16.783 --> 00:05:17.250
I mean, is

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:19.385
there can the Ukrainians produce

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:21.154
hundreds of thousands of drones?

00:05:21.154 --> 00:05:22.522
They have the money

00:05:22.522 --> 00:05:24.023
and they have the talent.

00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:24.991
They haven't figured out

00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:26.793
how to build all the factories yet.

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:28.161
And they have to be built in Ukraine

00:05:28.161 --> 00:05:29.696
for many, many reasons.

00:05:29.696 --> 00:05:30.930
So what I know is

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.398
there are about 60 companies

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:34.200
that are building these types of drones.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:35.034
What's interesting is

00:05:35.034 --> 00:05:36.536
it's just like startups

00:05:36.536 --> 00:05:37.070
in the sense

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:37.870
that they're not particularly

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:38.671
well coordinated.

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:39.706
They're moving so quickly.

00:05:39.706 --> 00:05:41.507
Remember, this is all a year old.

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:42.542
They're operating systems

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:44.010
and software aren't very integrated.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:45.445
They can't speak to each other.

00:05:45.445 --> 00:05:47.213
All the problems that you would imagine

00:05:47.213 --> 00:05:48.648
now, if it were peacetime,

00:05:48.648 --> 00:05:49.882
you'd have an overall strategy.

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:51.818
You get them organized and so forth.

00:05:51.818 --> 00:05:53.453
What's interesting to me

00:05:53.453 --> 00:05:55.188
is that this is both a broadband war,

00:05:55.188 --> 00:05:55.888
but it's also

00:05:55.888 --> 00:05:57.390
a technology war in the sense

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:58.658
that it's innovative

00:05:58.658 --> 00:06:00.827
and innovation occurs in small companies,

00:06:00.827 --> 00:06:02.295
not in the mode.

00:06:02.295 --> 00:06:03.863
The Ukrainians were interesting.

00:06:03.863 --> 00:06:05.398
I think you know as well

00:06:05.398 --> 00:06:06.366
that the

00:06:06.366 --> 00:06:07.367
Ukrainians set up

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:08.334
their drone operation

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:09.869
outside the military.

00:06:09.869 --> 00:06:12.038
And the drone guy's name is Fedorov

00:06:12.038 --> 00:06:14.040
is busy supplying them to the military,

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:15.308
but he controls the money.

00:06:15.308 --> 00:06:16.876
He controls the strategy.

00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:18.511
They told us that the biggest problem

00:06:18.511 --> 00:06:19.746
they currently have

00:06:19.746 --> 00:06:20.580
is that at the moment

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:21.147
they're taking these

00:06:21.147 --> 00:06:23.383
tiny little essentially pipe bombs

00:06:23.383 --> 00:06:25.151
and dropping them on to tanks.

00:06:25.151 --> 00:06:27.086
And what they want is laser guided ones

00:06:27.086 --> 00:06:28.020
or guided ones,

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:30.256
which is America's had for a long time.

00:06:30.256 --> 00:06:32.191
They can follow the target.

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:32.959
Again, this is stuff

00:06:32.959 --> 00:06:34.827
that America did 20 years ago

00:06:34.827 --> 00:06:36.496
that they're just catching up on.

00:06:36.496 --> 00:06:37.330
Did it does

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:38.664
does all this leave you

00:06:38.664 --> 00:06:40.900
net, net, positive, optimistic?

00:06:41.968 --> 00:06:42.301
I hate

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:42.769
to say it

00:06:42.769 --> 00:06:43.035
but I

00:06:43.035 --> 00:06:44.370
think this is going to go on

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:45.304
for a long time.

00:06:45.304 --> 00:06:47.106
There's not enough advantage

00:06:47.106 --> 00:06:48.174
on either side.

00:06:48.174 --> 00:06:50.910
I don't think Russia will gain much land,

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:51.711
if any.

00:06:51.711 --> 00:06:52.779
And I think the going

00:06:52.779 --> 00:06:53.880
is so slow

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:55.481
to get across this danger

00:06:55.481 --> 00:06:57.417
zone, this killing field,

00:06:57.417 --> 00:06:59.185
that it will take a year or two.

00:06:59.185 --> 00:07:00.153
Now, of course,

00:07:00.153 --> 00:07:01.087
there could be breakthroughs.

00:07:01.087 --> 00:07:02.188
There could be

00:07:02.188 --> 00:07:03.423
Wagner could start running

00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:04.590
and things like that that we don't

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:05.691
we don't understand.

00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:06.726
But at the moment,

00:07:06.726 --> 00:07:08.127
it's much more balanced

00:07:08.127 --> 00:07:09.962
than the marketing says.

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:11.864
They talk about this counteroffensive,

00:07:11.864 --> 00:07:13.766
which is certainly a great idea.

00:07:13.766 --> 00:07:15.301
They're not ready to do

00:07:15.301 --> 00:07:16.803
an American style.

00:07:16.803 --> 00:07:18.171
100 million people,

00:07:18.171 --> 00:07:20.072
you know, state, you know, full power.

00:07:20.072 --> 00:07:21.607
They don't have the assets.

00:07:21.607 --> 00:07:22.108
Furthermore,

00:07:22.108 --> 00:07:23.643
if you put airplanes in the air,

00:07:23.643 --> 00:07:24.911
they get shot down by Russian

00:07:24.911 --> 00:07:26.212
surface to air missiles.

00:07:26.212 --> 00:07:27.880
So it's a really hard problem.

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:29.415
One of my friends who was looking at

00:07:29.415 --> 00:07:30.950
this strategically said,

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:32.185
You realize that the Russians

00:07:32.185 --> 00:07:33.186
have been fighting this way

00:07:33.186 --> 00:07:35.221
for 100 years? I said, Okay.

00:07:35.221 --> 00:07:36.055
And he said,

00:07:36.055 --> 00:07:36.989
that means that you have

00:07:36.989 --> 00:07:38.991
to give them a hard problem to solve

00:07:39.592 --> 00:07:40.827
the simple problems, like

00:07:40.827 --> 00:07:41.994
do this and do that.

00:07:43.095 --> 00:07:45.264
The other side is too sophisticated.

00:07:45.264 --> 00:07:45.932
And the Russians

00:07:45.932 --> 00:07:48.501
are clearly in this to win

00:07:49.302 --> 00:07:50.970
Sobering, but but very smart.

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:52.171
Thank you. Eric Schmidt, thank you.

